To (hopefully) forestall more requests, I'm posting this to
net.sources.  Apparently people have received the windows library, but
can't find documentation.  I sent documentation before the first source
file.  It may have been eaten by someone's mailer; it was more than
65535 bytes.  If anyone needs it I can mail it out.  (Sorry folks, I
haven't made a man 3 page; there's just too much there.  Most of that
70K or so is on the functions.)

Also, one small note:  I've only tested windows on 4.1BSD and Unisoft
V7+ (ie V7 with 4.1 system calls and include files, but none of the 4.1
stuff works), so it probably won't work on Sys III or V without some
(hopefully quite small) changes to the code that uses stty()/gtty().

